              "deprecatedIds": [
                "CVE-2026-113661",
                "GHSA-cv27-6wvh-8x7j"
              ],
              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "### Summary\n\nCVE-2026-53606 expanded `allowedSchemesAppliedToAttributes` so named URL attributes (`action`, `formaction`, `data`, `poster`, `background`, later `ping`, `xlink:href`, …) go through `naughtyHref()`. A **URL nested inside `meta` `content`** (`http-equiv=refresh`) is not an attribute name on that list, so the embedded destination is never scheme-checked.\n\nDefault `allowedTags` still omit `meta`. Same non-default integrator config as 53606: allow `meta` plus `http-equiv` / `content`.\n\nOn **2.17.7**:\n\n```text\nsanitizeHtml(\n  '\u003cmeta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0;url=javascript:alert(1)\"\u003e',\n  { allowedTags: ['meta'], allowedAttributes: { meta: ['http-equiv', 'content'] } }\n)\n// =\u003e \u003cmeta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0;url=javascript:alert(1)\" /\u003e\n```\n\n`data:text/html,…` and arbitrary `https:` destinations also survive. `formaction=\"javascript:…\"` (53606) is stripped.\n\nPlease **Request CVE**. Credit: Finder + Reporter (`adrbogacz`).\n\n### Details\n\n`naughtyHref()` only runs when the attribute name is in `allowedSchemesAppliedToAttributes` (`index.js` ~385). Refresh URLs live in a `content` value of the form `0;url=…`, so the gate never fires. Adding `content` to that list wholesale would break ordinary meta `content` (description, viewport).\n\n**Fix:** when `http-equiv` is `refresh` (case-insensitive), parse the `; url=` destination and run `naughtyHref('meta', url)`. Drop `content` (or the tag) if the URL is rejected. Leave other `meta` `content` values alone.\n\n### PoC\n\nLocal `sanitize-html@2.17.7`. Output inspection only:\n\n```text\nnode -e '\nconst sanitize = require(\"sanitize-html\");\nconst opts = { allowedTags: [\"meta\"], allowedAttributes: { meta: [\"http-equiv\", \"content\"] } };\nfor (const html of [\n  \"\u003cmeta http-equiv=\\\"refresh\\\" content=\\\"0;url=javascript:alert(1)\\\"\u003e\",\n  \"\u003cmeta http-equiv=\\\"refresh\\\" content=\\\"0;url=data:text/html,aaa\\\"\u003e\",\n  \"\u003cform\u003e\u003cbutton formaction=\\\"javascript:alert(1)\\\"\u003ex\u003c/button\u003e\u003c/form\u003e\",\n]) {\n  console.log(html, \"=\u003e\", sanitize(html, html.includes(\"meta\") ? opts : { allowedTags: [\"form\",\"button\"], allowedAttributes: { button: [\"formaction\"] } }));\n}\n'\n```\n\nExpected: refresh `javascript:` / `data:` remain; 53606 `formaction` is removed. Do not attach a browser hang or stored-XSS page.\n\n### Impact\n\nAn integrator who allowed `meta` + `content` expecting `allowedSchemes` to apply (the 53606 configuration pattern) still emits a refresh to `javascript:`, `data:`, or an attacker `https:` URL. Stored XSS / open redirect for viewers of that HTML. Default config is not affected.",
                "text": "### Summary\n\nCVE-2026-53606 expanded `allowedSchemesAppliedToAttributes` so named URL attributes (`action`, `formaction`, `data`, `poster`, `background`, later `ping`, `xlink:href`, …) go through `naughtyHref()`. A **URL nested inside `meta` `content`** (`http-equiv=refresh`) is not an attribute name on that list, so the embedded destination is never scheme-checked.\n\nDefault `allowedTags` still omit `meta`. Same non-default integrator config as 53606: allow `meta` plus `http-equiv` / `content`.\n\nOn **2.17.7**:\n\n```text\nsanitizeHtml(\n  '\u003cmeta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0;url=javascript:alert(1)\"\u003e',\n  { allowedTags: ['meta'], allowedAttributes: { meta: ['http-equiv', 'content'] } }\n)\n// =\u003e \u003cmeta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0;url=javascript:alert(1)\" /\u003e\n```\n\n`data:text/html,…` and arbitrary `https:` destinations also survive. `formaction=\"javascript:…\"` (53606) is stripped.\n\nPlease **Request CVE**. Credit: Finder + Reporter (`adrbogacz`).\n\n### Details\n\n`naughtyHref()` only runs when the attribute name is in `allowedSchemesAppliedToAttributes` (`index.js` ~385). Refresh URLs live in a `content` value of the form `0;url=…`, so the gate never fires. Adding `content` to that list wholesale would break ordinary meta `content` (description, viewport).\n\n**Fix:** when `http-equiv` is `refresh` (case-insensitive), parse the `; url=` destination and run `naughtyHref('meta', url)`. Drop `content` (or the tag) if the URL is rejected. Leave other `meta` `content` values alone.\n\n### PoC\n\nLocal `sanitize-html@2.17.7`. Output inspection only:\n\n```text\nnode -e '\nconst sanitize = require(\"sanitize-html\");\nconst opts = { allowedTags: [\"meta\"], allowedAttributes: { meta: [\"http-equiv\", \"content\"] } };\nfor (const html of [\n  \"\u003cmeta http-equiv=\\\"refresh\\\" content=\\\"0;url=javascript:alert(1)\\\"\u003e\",\n  \"\u003cmeta http-equiv=\\\"refresh\\\" content=\\\"0;url=data:text/html,aaa\\\"\u003e\",\n  \"\u003cform\u003e\u003cbutton formaction=\\\"javascript:alert(1)\\\"\u003ex\u003c/button\u003e\u003c/form\u003e\",\n]) {\n  console.log(html, \"=\u003e\", sanitize(html, html.includes(\"meta\") ? opts : { allowedTags: [\"form\",\"button\"], allowedAttributes: { button: [\"formaction\"] } }));\n}\n'\n```\n\nExpected: refresh `javascript:` / `data:` remain; 53606 `formaction` is removed. Do not attach a browser hang or stored-XSS page.\n\n### Impact\n\nAn integrator who allowed `meta` + `content` expecting `allowedSchemes` to apply (the 53606 configuration pattern) still emits a refresh to `javascript:`, `data:`, or an attacker `https:` URL. Stored XSS / open redirect for viewers of that HTML. Default config is not affected."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-113661](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-113661)**.\n\n## [GHSA-cv27-6wvh-8x7j](https://osv.dev/GHSA-cv27-6wvh-8x7j)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e CVE-2026-53606 expanded `allowedSchemesAppliedToAttributes` so named URL attributes (`action`, `formaction`, `data`, `poster`, `background`, later `ping`, `xlink:href`, …) go through `naughtyHref()`. A **URL nested inside `meta` `content`** (`http-equiv=refresh`) is not an attribute name on that list, so the embedded destination is never scheme-checked.\n\u003e \n\u003e Default `allowedTags` still omit `meta`. Same non-default integrator config as 53606: allow `meta` plus `http-equiv` / `content`.\n\u003e \n\u003e On **2.17.7**:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e sanitizeHtml(\n\u003e   '\u003cmeta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0;url=javascript:alert(1)\"\u003e',\n\u003e   { allowedTags: ['meta'], allowedAttributes: { meta: ['http-equiv', 'content'] } }\n\u003e )\n\u003e // =\u003e \u003cmeta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0;url=javascript:alert(1)\" /\u003e\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e `data:text/html,…` and arbitrary `https:` destinations also survive. `formaction=\"javascript:…\"` (53606) is stripped.\n\u003e \n\u003e Please **Request CVE**. Credit: Finder + Reporter (`adrbogacz`).\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Details\n\u003e \n\u003e `naughtyHref()` only runs when the attribute name is in `allowedSchemesAppliedToAttributes` (`index.js` ~385). Refresh URLs live in a `content` value of the form `0;url=…`, so the gate never fires. Adding `content` to that list wholesale would break ordinary meta `content` (description, viewport).\n\u003e \n\u003e **Fix:** when `http-equiv` is `refresh` (case-insensitive), parse the `; url=` destination and run `naughtyHref('meta', url)`. Drop `content` (or the tag) if the URL is rejected. Leave other `meta` `content` values alone.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### PoC\n\u003e \n\u003e Local `sanitize-html@2.17.7`. Output inspection only:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e node -e '\n\u003e const sanitize = require(\"sanitize-html\");\n\u003e const opts = { allowedTags: [\"meta\"], allowedAttributes: { meta: [\"http-equiv\", \"content\"] } };\n\u003e for (const html of [\n\u003e   \"\u003cmeta http-equiv=\\\"refresh\\\" content=\\\"0;url=javascript:alert(1)\\\"\u003e\",\n\u003e   \"\u003cmeta http-equiv=\\\"refresh\\\" content=\\\"0;url=data:text/html,aaa\\\"\u003e\",\n\u003e   \"\u003cform\u003e\u003cbutton formaction=\\\"javascript:alert(1)\\\"\u003ex\u003c/button\u003e\u003c/form\u003e\",\n\u003e ]) {\n\u003e   console.log(html, \"=\u003e\", sanitize(html, html.includes(\"meta\") ? opts : { allowedTags: [\"form\",\"button\"], allowedAttributes: { button: [\"formaction\"] } }));\n\u003e }\n\u003e '\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e Expected: refresh `javascript:` / `data:` remain; 53606 `formaction` is removed. Do not attach a browser hang or stored-XSS page.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e An integrator who allowed `meta` + `content` expecting `allowedSchemes` to apply (the 53606 configuration pattern) still emits a refresh to `javascript:`, `data:`, or an attacker `https:` URL. Stored XSS / open redirect for viewers of that HTML. Default config is not affected.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/user/felipe/speckit/juice-shop-master/package-lock.json | sanitize-html | 1.4.2 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-cv27-6wvh-8x7j | sanitize-html | 2.18.0 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/user/felipe/speckit/juice-shop-master/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-113661\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2026-113661](https://osv.dev/CVE-2026-113661)**.\n\n## [GHSA-cv27-6wvh-8x7j](https://osv.dev/GHSA-cv27-6wvh-8x7j)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Summary\n\u003e \n\u003e CVE-2026-53606 expanded `allowedSchemesAppliedToAttributes` so named URL attributes (`action`, `formaction`, `data`, `poster`, `background`, later `ping`, `xlink:href`, …) go through `naughtyHref()`. A **URL nested inside `meta` `content`** (`http-equiv=refresh`) is not an attribute name on that list, so the embedded destination is never scheme-checked.\n\u003e \n\u003e Default `allowedTags` still omit `meta`. Same non-default integrator config as 53606: allow `meta` plus `http-equiv` / `content`.\n\u003e \n\u003e On **2.17.7**:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e sanitizeHtml(\n\u003e   '\u003cmeta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0;url=javascript:alert(1)\"\u003e',\n\u003e   { allowedTags: ['meta'], allowedAttributes: { meta: ['http-equiv', 'content'] } }\n\u003e )\n\u003e // =\u003e \u003cmeta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0;url=javascript:alert(1)\" /\u003e\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e `data:text/html,…` and arbitrary `https:` destinations also survive. `formaction=\"javascript:…\"` (53606) is stripped.\n\u003e \n\u003e Please **Request CVE**. Credit: Finder + Reporter (`adrbogacz`).\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Details\n\u003e \n\u003e `naughtyHref()` only runs when the attribute name is in `allowedSchemesAppliedToAttributes` (`index.js` ~385). Refresh URLs live in a `content` value of the form `0;url=…`, so the gate never fires. Adding `content` to that list wholesale would break ordinary meta `content` (description, viewport).\n\u003e \n\u003e **Fix:** when `http-equiv` is `refresh` (case-insensitive), parse the `; url=` destination and run `naughtyHref('meta', url)`. Drop `content` (or the tag) if the URL is rejected. Leave other `meta` `content` values alone.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### PoC\n\u003e \n\u003e Local `sanitize-html@2.17.7`. Output inspection only:\n\u003e \n\u003e ```text\n\u003e node -e '\n\u003e const sanitize = require(\"sanitize-html\");\n\u003e const opts = { allowedTags: [\"meta\"], allowedAttributes: { meta: [\"http-equiv\", \"content\"] } };\n\u003e for (const html of [\n\u003e   \"\u003cmeta http-equiv=\\\"refresh\\\" content=\\\"0;url=javascript:alert(1)\\\"\u003e\",\n\u003e   \"\u003cmeta http-equiv=\\\"refresh\\\" content=\\\"0;url=data:text/html,aaa\\\"\u003e\",\n\u003e   \"\u003cform\u003e\u003cbutton formaction=\\\"javascript:alert(1)\\\"\u003ex\u003c/button\u003e\u003c/form\u003e\",\n\u003e ]) {\n\u003e   console.log(html, \"=\u003e\", sanitize(html, html.includes(\"meta\") ? opts : { allowedTags: [\"form\",\"button\"], allowedAttributes: { button: [\"formaction\"] } }));\n\u003e }\n\u003e '\n\u003e ```\n\u003e \n\u003e Expected: refresh `javascript:` / `data:` remain; 53606 `formaction` is removed. Do not attach a browser hang or stored-XSS page.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e An integrator who allowed `meta` + `content` expecting `allowedSchemes` to apply (the 53606 configuration pattern) still emits a refresh to `javascript:`, `data:`, or an attacker `https:` URL. Stored XSS / open redirect for viewers of that HTML. Default config is not affected.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/user/felipe/speckit/juice-shop-master/package-lock.json | sanitize-html | 1.4.2 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-cv27-6wvh-8x7j | sanitize-html | 2.18.0 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/user/felipe/speckit/juice-shop-master/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2026-113661\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
